      { title:'Killing at experimental endpoints', context:'Some research protocols', description:'Primates may be euthanized when tissue collection is required or at defined endpoints. Other animals may be retained or rehomed where rules and circumstances allow.', welfare:'This is system- and protocol-dependent and should not be presented as universal for every primate study.', urls:[{label:'Evidence / welfare source',url:'https://www.nc3rs.org.uk/the-3rs'}] },
